NA: He looks at the papers on the table, touching one with the tip of his fingers.
TI: For some time, I have carried certain thoughts… certain intentions…
NA: He lifts his eyes to you.
TI: And for some reason… I believe you are capable of understanding them.
NA: He makes a subtle gesture, inviting you closer to the table.
@char {PLAYER}2.neutral
@char TI.determined look:left pos:{rightmid}
TI: Tell me… have you the resolve to hear the unrest of a man who can no longer live in peace under the yoke imposed upon us?
NA: His voice is low, but firm.

@choice "Tell me what you have in mind." goto:.scene3T-1
@choice "Perhaps, but I worry about the consequences of your plans." goto:.scene3T-2
@stop

# scene3T-1
@set afetoTiradentes+=1
NA: He holds your gaze for a moment. Then nods slightly.
@char TI.determined look:left pos:{rightmid}
TI: Very well.
NA: He opens one of the maps.
NA: The lines are carefully marked villages, roads, circled points.
TI: This land bleeds in silence.
NA: His fingers trace the map.
TI: The gold taken from here does not remain here. It is sent overseas, to sustain a Crown that knows nothing of our suffering.
TI: And when there is no longer enough gold…
NA: He tightens his grip slightly on the paper.
@char TI.angry look:left pos:{rightmid}
TI: They devise new ways to drain us. Taxes, levies… the Derrama.
NA: There is bitterness in his voice, but also something deeper.
TI: We are not subjects. We are resources.
NA: He takes a deep breath.
NA: For a moment, he seems more tired than ever.
@char TI.thinking look:left pos:{rightmid}
TI: There are men who think as I do. Men who believe this land can be free. That it can govern itself.
NA: He looks directly at you.
TI: Not out of ambition, but out of dignity.
NA: His eyes falter for a brief moment.
TI: Yet… it is no light burden.
NA: He runs a hand over his face, weary.
TI: Sleep has been scarce.
@char TI.neutral look:left pos:{rightmid}
TI: There are nights when I close my eyes and see only what may go wrong.
@char {PLAYER}2.thinking look:left pos:{leftmid}
PLAYER: (I could give you a spoiler…)
NA: He exhales softly almost a humorless laugh.
TI: Failure would not condemn only me… but all those who dare to believe.
@char {PLAYER}2.thinking look:left pos:{leftmid}
PLAYER: (If you had access to my history books… you might disagree.)
NA: He looks back at you.
TI: Even so… there are moments when a single presence is enough to ease the burden.
NA: A pause.
TI: Tell me.
NA: His voice is softer now.
@char TI.thinking look:left pos:{rightmid}
TI: What do you think of all this?
@goto #scene3T-1end

# scene3T-2
NA: Silence weighs after your words.
TI: Consequences…
NA: He repeats the word slowly, as if tasting it.
NA: His expression shifts, subtly.
TI: Prudence is a rare virtue in these times.
NA: He walks to the window, glancing outside for a moment, making sure you are alone.
NA: When he speaks again, his voice is measured.
@char TI.thinking look:left pos:{rightmid}
TI: Suppose… merely as an exercise of thought… that some men in this captaincy consider rising against the Crown’s abuses.
NA: He does not say it as a confession.
@char TI.determined look:left pos:{rightmid}
TI: Suppose such men have grown weary of the Derrama, of the royal fifth, and of constant humiliation.
TI: And that they believe the time has come to govern this land according to their own interests.
NA: He stops before you, carefully studying your expression.
@char TI.thinking look:left pos:{rightmid}
TI: What would you say of such men?
NA: There is no lightness now.
TI: Would you call them reckless? Traitors? Or courageous?
NA: He steps closer.
TI: Because consequences… yes, they do exist.
@char {PLAYER}2.determined look:left pos:{leftmid}
PLAYER: Have you truly considered what those consequences might be?
NA: His voice lowers even further.
@char TI.sad look:left pos:{rightmid}
TI: Imprisonment. Confiscation of property. A public example.
NA: A brief flicker crosses his eyes something he has already imagined for himself.
@char {PLAYER}2.angry look:left pos:{leftmid}
PLAYER: "A public example”… have you at least considered the possibility of your mission being suici...
@char {PLAYER}2.determined
NA: You stop yourself.
@char TI.determined look:left pos:{rightmid}
TI: And yet… there are consequences in doing nothing as well.
NA: He crosses his arms.
TI: To live forever under unjust taxes… to watch the people suffer and remain still.
TI: So tell me.
NA: His tone is almost calm.
@char TI.thinking look:left pos:{rightmid}
TI: Which consequence seems more dreadful to you?

# scene3T-1end
NA: You meet his gaze, thinking about what to say.
NA: There is tension in the air, as if your answer carries weight.
NA: Tiradentes does not look away.
NA: The silence grows between you.
NA: You take a breath, about to speak but your hand hits the edge of the table, knocking over a glass of water.
